From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:20:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 142/161] hjviewer: the system's text size on phones, up to 130
 % (UX-K3)

UX-K3 (U58): a phone or tablet follows the system's text size from 100 %
to 130 % (MediaQuery's scaler clamped, so a larger or non-linear size
stops at 130 % of each font size); a desktop stays at 100 % (T5). The
new common/hjv_text_scale.dart holds the bounds and the builders:
main.dart's Android builder and its iOS branch take
hjvTextScaleBuilder; the desktop branch keeps _keepScaleBuilder. The
phone's remote screen (with its key bar and gesture guide) and its
terminal stay at 100 % (hjvFixedTextScale); the dialogs they open are
above them, in the app's scale.

Room for the larger text first: the phone ID field is at least 84 high
instead of 84, and its AutoSizeTextField, which scaled the ID once in
its fit and once more in its TextField, sits at 1.0 with its sizes
scaled once; the peer bar's pills and search field are at least 32
high; a phone's menu rows (popup_menu.dart) grow past the menu's row
height, a desktop's keep it; the settings side bar's tabs are at least
40 high; HjvDialogTitle and a callout's one-line title take two lines
on a phone (one on a desktop).

Tests: test/hjviewer_text_scale_test.dart (the bounds on a phone and a
desktop, a non-linear size, the app's builder and the 100 % wrapper,
the menu row's box, a card's title at 130 % on a 320 px phone).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
